---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Intended Use -- 24K Labs" description="What 24K Labs' AI services are designed for, what they must not be used for, and their known limitations.">

  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="page-header__glow"></div>
    <div class="container">
      <span class="page-header__badge">Legal</span>
      <h1 class="page-header__title">Intended Use</h1>
      <p class="page-header__desc">
        What these services are for, what they are not for, and where they fall short.
        Forty seconds to read. Worth it before you wire us into anything.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose reveal">

        <p>
          <strong>Effective date:</strong> September 3, 2026.
          This statement forms part of our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What These Services Are For</h2>
        <p>
          Explaining, debugging, reviewing and security-auditing source code, for developers
          and engineers working on their own projects. That is what these services were
          designed for and what they have been tested against.
        </p>

        <h2>What They Are Not For</h2>
        <p>
          These services must not be used to make, or materially inform, decisions about people.
          The following are explicitly out of scope:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Employment, recruitment, or worker management</li>
          <li>Credit scoring or assessment of creditworthiness</li>
          <li>Access to education or vocational training</li>
          <li>Medical, clinical, or healthcare decisions</li>
          <li>Insurance pricing or eligibility</li>
          <li>Law enforcement, migration, asylum, or border control</li>
          <li>Biometric identification, categorisation, or emotion inference</li>
          <li>Assessing a person's eligibility for essential public or private services</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We have not built, tested, or validated for any of these, and we do not support them.
          If your use case is on that list, these are the wrong tools and we would rather tell
          you now than take the payment.
        </p>

        <h2>Known Limitations</h2>
        <p>
          Output quality varies by model tier and by how much context you send. The analysis sees
          only what is in your request -- it has no knowledge of your wider codebase, your runtime
          environment, your dependencies, or your business rules unless you include them.
        </p>
        <p>
          It can be <strong>confidently wrong</strong>. A plausible, well-written answer is not the
          same as a correct one, and the system cannot reliably tell you which one you just got.
          Every result is advisory and needs a human read before it is acted on.
        </p>

        <h2>Who The User Is</h2>
        <p>
          Developers, engineers, and automated agents acting on their behalf. Not consumers,
          and not people being evaluated by the output.
        </p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>
          Anything about this statement, including inquiries under the EU AI Act, goes to
          <a href="mailto:sean@24klabs.ai">sean@24klabs.ai</a>.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
